# ---------------- Benin Bronzes ----------------
meta={
"type":"object","title_zh":"贝宁青铜：宫殿、远征与归还","title_en":"The Benin Bronzes: Palace, Punitive Expedition, and Return",
"era":"约 13–19 世纪；1897 年流散","era_en":"c. 13th–19th centuries; dispersed in 1897",
"region":"尼日利亚，埃多州，贝宁城","region_en":"Benin City, Edo State, Nigeria",
"coords":[6.335,5.626],"tags":["贝宁青铜","尼日利亚","贝宁王国","归还","殖民"],"collections":[],"credibility":"verified",
"related":["jade-burial-suit","tutankhamun-mask"],
"en_headings":["A palace workshop","The 1897 expedition","Dispersal into museums","The return debate","Casting and material","What restitution changes"],
"limits_zh":"“贝宁青铜”是一个集合名称，包含 plaque、头像、人物像、象牙与金属器物，年代跨越数百年，制作作坊也不止一处。1897 年远征中究竟有多少件被带走，各馆藏品与档案的数字并不一致；有些器物后来经过多次转手、拍卖和私人收藏。归还的法律路径因国家而异，欧盟与英国的博物馆法、尼日利亚的收藏政策并不统一。本文把可核对的远征记录、馆藏编号与已完成的归还分开陈述。",
"limits_en":"'Benin Bronzes' is a collective label covering plaques, heads, figures, ivory, and metalwork made over several centuries in more than one workshop. How many objects were taken in the 1897 expedition is uncertain, and museum holdings and archival counts do not agree; some pieces passed through several owners, auctions, and private collections. Legal routes to return differ by country, and EU, UK museum law, and Nigerian collection policy are not uniform. This entry separates checkable expedition records, museum numbers, and completed returns.",
}
sections=[
("一、宫殿里的作坊","贝宁王国以今天的尼日利亚贝宁城为中心，从 13 世纪前后延续到 19 世纪末。宫廷作坊为 oba（国王）制作青铜与黄铜器物：宫殿墙上的浮雕 plaque、祖先头像、仪式用的人物与动物、象牙与珊瑚饰物。这些器物不是单纯的“艺术品”，它们记录王权、战功、祭祀和外来贸易，安放在宫殿、祭坛和仪式的具体位置。","The kingdom of Benin was centred on what is now Benin City in Nigeria and lasted from around the thirteenth century to the end of the nineteenth. Palace workshops made bronze and brass objects for the oba: relief plaques on palace walls, ancestor heads, ritual figures and animals, ivory and coral ornaments. These were not simply 'art objects'; they recorded kingship, military success, sacrifice, and foreign trade, and were placed at specific points in palaces, altars, and ceremonies."),
("二、1897 年的远征","1897 年，英国以一名官员在前往贝宁城途中被杀为由，发动“贝宁惩罚远征”。英军攻入贝宁城，焚烧宫殿与城镇，掠走大量青铜、象牙和皇家器物。oba Ovonramwen 被废黜并流放。这次行动不是一次普通考古发掘，而是殖民战争中的系统性掠夺；后来的收藏、拍卖和博物馆入藏，都建立在这一节点上。","In 1897 Britain launched the 'Benin Punitive Expedition', citing the killing of an official on the way to Benin City. British forces entered the city, burned palaces and town areas, and removed large quantities of bronze, ivory, and royal objects. The oba, Ovonramwen, was deposed and exiled. This was not an ordinary archaeological excavation but systematic looting in a colonial war; later collections, auctions, and museum accessions all rest on this event."),
("三、流散与馆藏","掠走的器物被分给参与行动的军官和英国政府，随后通过拍卖进入大英博物馆、柏林民族学博物馆、纽约大都会艺术博物馆等机构。今天“贝宁青铜”分散在欧美多家博物馆和私人收藏中，部分器物直到 20 世纪后期才被重新编目。来源研究（provenance）因此成为关键：一件器物的入藏记录、拍卖目录和经手人，往往比展签上的“贝宁”二字更能说明它如何离开尼日利亚。","The removed objects were distributed to officers and the British government, then entered institutions such as the British Museum, the Berlin Ethnological Museum, and the Metropolitan Museum of Art through auctions. Today the 'Benin Bronzes' are scattered across European and American museums and private collections, and some were only recatalogued late in the twentieth century. Provenance research is therefore central: an object's accession record, auction catalogue, and chain of owners often explain how it left Nigeria better than the label 'Benin' on a display case."),
("四、归还的路径","尼日利亚自 20 世纪中期以来持续要求归还。1970 年代，部分器物被移交给尼日利亚；2021–2022 年，德国与英国的多家机构开始归还或转移所有权，史密森尼学会也采取了类似行动。归还并不统一：有的国家受博物馆法限制，只能长期借展；有的机构选择“共同保管”或数字共享。围绕“普世博物馆”与“来源国权利”的争论，至今没有全球一致的规则。","Nigeria has sought return since the mid-twentieth century. Some objects were transferred in the 1970s; in 2021–2022 several German and British institutions began returning or transferring title, and the Smithsonian took similar steps. Returns are not uniform: some countries are constrained by museum law and can offer only long-term loans; others choose 'shared custody' or digital access. The argument between 'universal museums' and 'source-country rights' still has no globally consistent rule."),
("五、工艺与材料","这些器物多为黄铜（铜锌合金），而非严格意义上的“青铜”（铜锡合金）；“Bronze”一词是历史形成的统称。制作使用失蜡法：先以蜡制模，覆泥成壳，加热使蜡流出，再浇入金属。plaque 的浮雕细节、头像的铸造厚度和表面包浆，都是判断年代与作坊的线索。它们与 Ife 的铸造传统、跨撒哈拉贸易和欧洲货物之间存在联系，不能孤立看待。","Most of these objects are brass (a copper-zinc alloy) rather than strict 'bronze' (copper-tin); 'Bronze' is a historical collective term. They were made by lost-wax casting: a wax model was coated in clay, heated so the wax ran out, and molten metal poured in. The relief detail of plaques, the casting thickness of heads, and surface patina are clues to date and workshop. They connect to the casting tradition of Ife, trans-Saharan trade, and European goods, and cannot be understood in isolation."),
("六、归还之后","归还的器物需要新的保存、研究和展示条件。尼日利亚计划在贝宁城建设博物馆，并在宫殿与遗址中重新安置部分作品；但电力、气候控制、安保和人员培训仍是现实问题。归还也不是终点：它改变的是所有权和叙事权，接下来要回答的是，谁有权解释这些器物，以及观众能否在它们被制作的地方看到它们。","Returned objects need new conditions for conservation, research, and display. Nigeria plans a museum in Benin City and the reinstallation of some works in palaces and sites; electricity, climate control, security, and staff training remain practical issues. Return is not an endpoint: it changes ownership and the right to narrate. The next questions are who has the authority to interpret these objects, and whether audiences can see them where they were made."),
]
